{"parentUuid":"935506e4-1542-42bb-ba1e-77911ba3ebab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Vb153r8wKkc1YrkguLG9xE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Same single bug. The footer prints from `fix.go:618`, called at `cmd.go:661` — but it sits **inside** `writePostReviewManifest`, after the early return at `cmd.go:653` (`if len(manifest.Sources) == 0 { return }`). Schematically:\n\n```\nwritePostReviewManifest:\n  if cancelled or 0 runs        → return            cmd.go:645\n  build manifest from state                          cmd.go:648\n  if manifest.Sources == 0      → return  ← YOU HIT THIS\n  write manifest                                     cmd.go:657\n  writeReviewCompletionFooter ← never reached       cmd.go:661\n```\n\n`Sources` is built only from session-state files where `Kind == \"agent_review\"` (`manifest.go:104`). Since the env-var handshake never tagged today's review sessions (the `os.Getenv(\"ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION\") != \"1\"` silent return in `lifecycle.go:1042`), `Sources` is empty, the manifest write skips, **and** the footer skips. The missing `--fix` hint and the empty `--findings` list are the same symptom of the same bug.\n\nSo: one broken upstream (env propagation from `entire review` → agent CLI → hook subprocess), three downstream features that all silently no-op (manifest persistence, `--findings` browsing, end-of-run footer hint). Nothing in the user-visible review output ever announces the failure — exactly the silent-failure pattern this codebase's own anti-features list and `superpowers:silent-failure-hunter` agent are designed to catch.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- This is a textbook case of a \"feature trio with one shared dependency\" failing as a unit. The author bundled manifest write, footer print, and findings list all behind `Kind == \"agent_review\"` filtering — sensible factoring, but it means a single upstream regression silently kills three user-visible features at once. A defensive design would have decoupled the footer (print whenever ≥1 agent succeeded) from manifest persistence (gate on `Kind` match if you must), so at minimum the user gets the next-step nudge even if the manifest can't be persisted.\n- The `lifecycle.go:1042` silent return is the bridge between the visible bug (no footer, no findings) and the invisible cause (env not propagating). That single line is the highest-leverage fix in the whole feature: changing it to log \"review env not detected at hook time\" at INFO would have made this a 30-second diagnosis instead of an hour of code spelunking. Worth filing as the smallest possible follow-up PR independent of the broader env-propagation fix.\n- Worth checking whether your local `claude` CLI version is sanitizing env for hooks — Anthropic's `claude` has historically had a hook-env passthrough policy that varied between versions; if a recent claude release tightened that, every `entire review` user gets this bug regardless of CLI version, which would explain why a feature that shipped in #1145 with passing tests now no-ops in the wild.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":113830,"output_tokens":1404,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1313,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":113830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1313},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqXpz4yMfvpjVXjTTrrN","type":"assistant","uuid":"a7090541-462d-425e-83a0-e14ced975147","timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:56:20.958Z","userType":"external","entrypoint"