{"parentUuid":"5aae8742-f563-4727-aa51-12b4f37ad3f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HE3hsvCtGKHg8EfWgWVUUS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three real issues in your report — let me triage:\n\n**1. The script is broken — my recipe's fault.**\n\nThat bash error in your stderr (`Authentication failed. Run claude login.: command not found`) is the fake binary itself failing to parse. Either fish's `printf` quoting got mangled in your shell, or copy-paste broke something. Switch to a more robust recipe that doesn't depend on escape interpretation:\n\n```fish\nmkdir -p /tmp/fake-bin\necho '#!/bin/bash' > /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'echo \"Error: invalid_api_key\" >&2' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'echo \"Authentication failed. Run claude login.\" >&2' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'echo \"Hint: see docs.claude.com/cli/auth\" >&2' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'exit 1' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\nchmod +x /tmp/fake-bin/claude\n```\n\nVerify: `/tmp/fake-bin/claude; echo \"exit: $status\"` — should show three clean stderr lines, no bash errors, `exit: 1`.\n\n**2. \"✓ done\" instead of \"✗ failed\" in the dashboard — bigger bug than my PR currently fixes.**\n\nYou spotted something my fix doesn't address. Look at this from your output:\n\n```\nclaude-code           ✓ done      2ms\n1 agent(s) done — 0 succeeded, 1 failed, 0 cancelled\n```\n\nThe row says `✓ done`, the tally says `1 failed`. Inconsistent. Here's why:\n\nWhen `claude` (your fake) exits, the parser reads stdout to EOF and emits `Finished{Success: true}` because it saw a clean stream close — the parser doesn't know about the exit code. The TUI marks the row Succeeded based on that event. The orchestrator then calls `proc.Wait()`, gets the non-zero exit + stderr (a `*ProcessError`), and classifies the run as Failed in the final summary. The TUI's `runFinishedMsg` handler explicitly *preserves* the parser's Succeeded marking and only updates Unknown rows — so the row stays ✓ done forever.\n\nFor multi-agent this is much worse than your fast smoke test made visible: claude fails in 2ms, codex runs for 7 minutes, the dashboard shows claude as `✓ done` for the whole 7 minutes. Exactly the \"shouldn't give them nothing\" complaint.\n\nThe real fix needs the orchestrator to emit a synthetic `RunError{waitErr}` event into the sink stream right after `proc.Wait()` returns a non-nil error. The TUI already handles `RunError` correctly (sets row.status=Failed, row.err=waitErr), so the live preview I added would then fire. This needs ~10 lines added to `run.go` and `run_multi.go`, plus a small dedup in `dump.go` so the same error doesn't render twice.\n\n**3. Dump rendering \"looks bad\" — partly from the broken script, partly real.**\n\nYour output shows weirdness like `Hint: see\\n  docs.claude.com/cli/auth` wrapping mid-URL. Some of that is glamour's terminal-width wrapping inside the code fence — unavoidable on narrow terminals, but tolerable. The bigger ugliness in your output is the bash syntax error inside the stderr block (`line 4: Authentication failed...: command not found`), which is from the broken fake binary, not the rendering. With a working fake, the fenced block reads clean.\n\n**4. \"Is the only error you checked for api error?\"**\n\nNo, the fix is generic. The `*ProcessError` type captures any process exit failure with stderr, regardless of *what* the agent's stderr says (auth errors, network timeouts, license issues, segfaults that emit stack traces, etc.). All of them get the fenced-block rendering. Anything *not* a `*ProcessError` (e.g., a generic `errors.New(...)` from somewhere upstream) keeps the inline rendering — backward compatible with the four existing failure-rendering tests.\n\n**Next step**\n\nThe \"✓ done despite failure\" bug (#2 above) is what's actually biting you in the multi-agent scenario. My current PR doesn't fix it. I'd recommend extending this PR to also emit synthetic `RunError` from the post-`Wait()` path so the TUI flips to ✗ failed live, mid-run. ~30-40 lines including a test, same TDD discipline.\n\nWant me to extend the PR? Or ship what we have (which fixes the post-run dump and the parser-emitted-RunError live case) and tackle the wait-error-live propagation in a follow-up?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1790,"cache_read_input_tokens":357323,"output_tokens":20982,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1790,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":20982,"cache_read_input_tokens":357323,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1790},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caqjkb9NEcReWZCBBJZKc","type":"assistant","uuid":"d82b3ff3-c681-480c-a3c2-36fbd33255ba","timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:36:57.366Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"802b09ab-4617-4518-902c-87ed5837e8f3","version":"2.1.133","gitBranch":"main"}
