{"parentUuid":"9f4fe4c4-9188-4235-869a-2f6a42793192","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VEmCjomSSd1GBJo63YJBUd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed working as intended in your output — `✗ failed` with error in preview while codex still running. ✓\n\nTo your question: **no, it captures any non-zero process exit, not just auth.** The auth message in your fake binary was illustrative; the actual mechanism is generic.\n\nThe fix triggers whenever `proc.Wait()` returns a non-nil error, which happens for *any* non-zero exit code. That includes the realistic agent failure modes:\n\n| Failure mode | Exit behavior | Captured? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Auth / API key invalid | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| Network timeout | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| Rate limit hit | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| Quota / license exceeded | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| Wrong model name | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| File permission errors | non-zero + stderr | ✓ |\n| Segfault / crash | non-zero (signal exit) + partial stderr | ✓ |\n| OOM killed | non-zero (137) + maybe no stderr | ✓ (header without fenced block) |\n| Torn stdout mid-response | parser RunError (already existed) | ✓ |\n| Scanner error mid-read | parser RunError (already existed) | ✓ |\n| Process exits 0 silently | nothing | ✗ |\n| Process hangs forever | nothing until you Ctrl+C | ✗ (cancellation path) |\n\nWhatever the agent CLI prints to stderr before exiting non-zero ends up in the live preview and the post-run fenced block. So a network timeout reads `error: codex: exit status 1: stderr: Connection timed out…` in the preview live, with full multi-line stderr (DNS hint, retry suggestion, etc.) in the dump.\n\n**The two failure modes NOT captured** are both edge cases:\n1. *Silent success* — agent exits 0 but produces no useful output. Looks like a clean run with empty narrative. Rare in practice; agents either output review findings or fail loudly.\n2. *Hung process* — never exits, you Ctrl+C to cancel. That goes through the cancellation path (`AgentStatusCancelled`), separate UX from failure.\n\nSo in practice this should surface essentially all failures users actually hit. The auth-style stderr in your test is just one shape — the same code path renders any other stderr shape identically.\n\nIf you want extra confidence, swap the fake binary's stderr to simulate a different real-world error and re-run — the rendering will be identical:\n\n```fish\necho '#!/bin/bash' > /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'echo \"Error: rate limit exceeded (RPS quota)\" >&2' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'echo \"Retry after: 47s\" >&2' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\necho 'exit 1' >> /tmp/fake-bin/claude\nenv PATH=/tmp/fake-bin:(string join : $PATH) /tmp/entire-failtest review --agent claude-code\n```\n\nSame flow, different message — and the preview should show `error: claude-code: exit status 1: stderr: Error: rate limit exceeded…` instead of the auth one. If that works, we have generic coverage.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The right framing for \"does X cover all cases?\" questions is to look at the *abstraction level* of the trigger condition, not the example. My trigger is \"process exit non-zero\" which is an abstract category covering thousands of concrete failure shapes; the auth message was just one shape I picked for the smoke test fixture. This is the same reason `*ProcessError` itself is generic — it captures `*exec.ExitError + stderr` regardless of what caused the exit code, which is the level at which \"everything that fails this way\" can be uniformly handled.\n- Worth noting that the *one* class of failures the fix can't reach — silent successes (exit 0 with empty narrative) — is also a failure mode users could legitimately confuse with success. If an agent gets booted off mid-thought by an auth refresh and exits cleanly, you'd see \"✓ done\" with no findings rendered. That's a separate problem from this PR but worth a future ticket: detect \"exit 0 with zero AssistantText events\" and surface a \"review produced no output\" warning.\n- Also worth naming: the failure mode you'd want to ABSOLUTELY catch — agents lying about success — isn't in this category. Claude-code or codex returning a successful exit code with bogus content (hallucinated findings, wrong scope, etc.) is a content-quality issue not a process-failure issue. Process-level fixes can't help; you'd need response validation or cross-checking, which is much further afield.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_read_input_tokens":414860,"output_tokens":3406,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3406,"cache_read_input_tokens":414860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqmKU2XWzP6dfsL2STKE","type":"assistant","uuid":"03081de2-d2e6-4f12-8c07-28d6d2dd14a2","timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:53:42.101Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"802b09ab-4617-4518-902c-87ed5837e8f3","version":"2.1.133","gitBranch":"main"}
