{"parentUuid":"60f8bf7a-c247-4cf6-bbba-0fe3c08fafd4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016xQwLqDYudA9zRjjqABR6e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y47QGMh6Qdm5PrXjGWeasg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --title \"feat(review): surface agent failures in live dashboard and post-run dump\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThree coordinated changes that make agent failures legible to the user instead of silently displayed as `✓ done` or buried inside an inline-code span:\n\n1. **`run.go` / `run_multi.go`** — emit a synthetic `RunError` event into the live sink stream when `proc.Wait()` returns a non-nil error, so failures reach the TUI mid-run instead of only via the final `RunFinished` summary. Without this, in a multi-agent run a fast-failing agent shows `✓ done` for the entire duration of any other still-running agent (the parser's clean-EOF `Finished{Success:true}` doesn't reflect the actual exit code).\n2. **`tui_model.go`** — when a row has failed and `row.err` is set, surface the error in the dashboard PREVIEW column instead of leaving it blank. New `formatErrorPreview` helper strips wrapper noise: for `*ProcessError` it returns the first non-empty stderr line directly (the agent CLI's headline message), since agent name and `✗ failed` status are already shown in adjacent columns. Generic errors render verbatim.\n3. **`dump.go`** — when `run.Err` is a `*ProcessError` carrying captured stderr, render the failure block as `**Failed:** \\`agent\\` exited (\\`exit status N\\`). Stderr:` followed by the full stderr in a fenced code block. Multi-line agent output (auth errors, retry hints, stack traces) reads cleanly. Synthetic `RunError` events whose `Err` matches `run.Err` are skipped from the blockquote loop to avoid double-printing.\n\n## Background\n\nUser-reported issue: when one agent in a multi-agent review fails, the dashboard shows `✗ failed` (or worse, `✓ done` due to the parser/exit-code mismatch) with an empty PREVIEW column for the entire remaining run duration. The post-run dump did show the failure, but only after dismissing the TUI — meaning during a 7-minute codex run, the user couldn't tell why claude had failed 2 minutes in. The dump rendering also crammed multi-line stderr into a single inline-code span, making it visually unreadable even after dismissal.\n\nThis change makes failures legible at three different points:\n- **Live dashboard**: PREVIEW column shows the first stderr line (truncated with `…` per terminal width)\n- **Ctrl+O drill-in**: same `RunError` event surfaces in the event buffer (truncation limitation noted below — separate ticket)\n- **Post-run dump**: full stderr in a fenced code block, no truncation\n\n## Coverage\n\nThe trigger is `proc.Wait()` returning non-nil — covers any non-zero process exit:\n\n| Failure mode | Captured? |\n|---|---|\n| Auth / API key invalid | ✓ |\n| Network timeout | ✓ |\n| Rate limit hit | ✓ |\n| Quota / license exceeded | ✓ |\n| Wrong model name | ✓ |\n| File permission errors | ✓ |\n| Segfault / signal kill | ✓ |\n| OOM kill (no stderr) | ✓ (header without fenced block) |\n| Torn stdout mid-response | ✓ (existing parser-emitted RunError, unchanged) |\n| Process exits 0 silently | ✗ (separate concern — empty-narrative detection) |\n| Process hangs forever | ✗ (cancellation path) |\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- Doesn't fix Ctrl+O drill-in truncation (`tui_detail.go:eventLine` still truncates each event to terminal width). The dashboard preview is more readable for the failure case but the detail view is unchanged. **Separate ticket** — needs proper viewport scrolling/wrapping.\n- Doesn't fix scope detection picking wrong base branch (bug confirmed structural — reproduces in fresh repos that never checked out the offending branch). **Next priority after this lands.**\n- Doesn't detect \"silent success\" (agent exits 0 with empty narrative). The trigger is non-zero exit; clean-exit-with-no-output cases are unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `mise run fmt` clean\n- [x] `mise run lint` — 0 issues\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/` passes (incl. 9 new tests, every one written first and watched fail before implementation)\n- [x] `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/` passes\n- [x] Manual smoke test: fake `claude` binary that exits non-zero with multi-line stderr, run via `env PATH=/tmp/fake-bin:$PATH entire review`. Verified:\n  - Dashboard row flips from running to `✗ failed` within milliseconds with first stderr line in preview\n  - Codex row continues running normally\n  - Post-run dump shows fenced block with all stderr lines readable\n  - Tested both auth-error and network-timeout shapes — same rendering, different message\n\n## Tests added\n\nProduction-code tests:\n- `TestDumpSink_FailedAgentWithProcessErrorRendersStderrAsCodeFence`\n- `TestDumpSink_DoesNotDoublePrintSyntheticRunErrorMatchingRunErr`\n- `TestTUIModel_DashboardShowsErrorPreviewForFailedAgent`\n- `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewYieldsToAssistantTextBeforeFailure`\n- `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewStripsProcessErrorWrapper`\n- `TestTUIModel_DashboardErrorPreviewFallsBackToErrStringForNonProcessError`\n- `TestRun_EmitsSyntheticRunErrorWhenWaitErrIsNonNil`\n- `TestRun_DoesNotEmitSyntheticRunErrorOnCleanExit`\n- `TestRunMulti_EmitsSyntheticRunErrorWhenAgentWaitErrIsNonNil`\n\nOne existing test updated for the new event-count contract:\n- `TestRunMulti_OneSucceedsOneFails`: failing agent now produces +1 event (the synthetic RunError) compared to before.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Open PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":456811,"output_tokens":2277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"s