{"parentUuid":"8df1edb3-c5dc-4d87-87e7-8586a1e85d49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZKrJGREn4xfriPkxA5Vth","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This PR fixes bug #4 (scope detection picking wrong base) plus three related issues that surfaced during smoke testing. All changes live in `cmd/entire/cli/review/`.\n\n**Four behavioral changes:**\n\n1. **Default scope is mainline, not \"closest merged ancestor\"** — replaces the timestamp heuristic that was picking unrelated recently-merged feature branches (`origin/soph/add-codex-post-tool` etc.) as the review base. New default walks the fallback chain `origin/main → origin/master → main → master`. Deleted ~130 lines of heuristic code (`slowDetectScopeBaseRef`, `isAncestorOf`, candidate selection loop).\n\n2. **`--base <ref>` flag for explicit override** — accepts any rev-parse-able ref (branch, tag, SHA). Validates with `git rev-parse --verify` before spawning agents so a typo errors immediately instead of after a 10-min review run. Stacked PR review (`--base feat/parent`) is now an explicit user action, not an inferred heuristic.\n\n3. **Uncommitted changes are now in scope** — scope clause changed from `\"review only the commits unique to this branch vs <ref>.\"` to `\"review the commits unique to this branch vs <ref>, plus any uncommitted changes in the working tree.\"` Agents (codex confirmed in smoke test) now review your in-progress work, not just committed commits. Checkpoint context preserved as a separate prompt section.\n\n4. **Three-dot diff in `countFilesChanged`** — was using `git diff base..HEAD` which over-counts files when mainline has advanced past the branch point (upstream-only changes appear as reversed deltas). Now uses `base...HEAD` (merge-base diff). Caught by codex during smoke; one-character fix in production code, no test could reliably reproduce it through testutil.\n\n**Tests added/changed:**\n\n- `TestDetectScopeBaseRef_PrefersMainOverAncestorBranches` — replaces `TestDetectScopeBaseRef_ClosestAncestorPreferred` (old test asserted opposite behavior)\n- `TestComputeScopeStats_BaseOverrideUsed` / `_BaseOverrideUnknownRefErrors` / `_EmptyOverrideUsesMainlineDetection` — three new unit tests for the override path\n- `TestComposeReviewPrompt_ScopeIncludesUncommittedChanges` — asserts the new scope clause wording\n- `TestReviewCommandSmoke_BaseFlagThreadsThroughToPromptAndBanner` / `_BadBaseRefErrorsBeforeAgentSpawn` — two command-level tests that catch wiring bugs (would have caught the `silentErr` suppression bug I had to fix mid-smoke)\n- Deleted `TestIsAncestorOf` (function deleted) and an attempted upstream-advance test that didn't actually reproduce the bug\n\n**Smoke-verified end-to-end:**\n\n- Banner shows `vs origin/main` not `vs origin/soph/add-codex-post-tool` ✓\n- `--base no-such-ref` errors with exit code 1 and message naming the bad ref ✓\n- Codex reviewed actual uncommitted scope.go/cmd.go/prompt.go changes (not just committed commits) ✓\n- Codex's review itself found two real issues in this PR (three-dot fix + missing command-level test, both now addressed) ✓\n\n**Net diff:** +43 lines (heuristic deletion outweighs flag wiring + tests), 6 files.\n\n**What this PR does NOT do** (worth calling out in PR description):\n- Doesn't change behavior for repos where mainline doesn't exist (fallback chain handles)\n- Doesn't add a persistent default in settings — `--base` is per-invocation\n- Doesn't touch `runGit` or other scope helpers\n- Doesn't address the still-open Ctrl+O drill-in truncation (separate ticket)\n\nReady to commit + push + open PR?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":597059,"output_tokens":1661,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":518,"ephemeral_